Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-28-2000||10:34 PM||||Earlier this year I tried to make some gauge stickers of my own, and they didn't turn out well at all... they looked horrible.<BR>they printed fine on regular paper, but when I printed them on the sticker paper, the ink looked like a "crackle finish"... <P>Until I can get some digital gauges, I want some cool black-faced stickers.. I never really liked the white faced ones, they look cheap IMHO...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>(no offense intended to anyone who sells, makes or uses white faced gauge stickers... there are lots of people who do like them, so don't take my comments personally.. hehehe)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||12-28-2000||10:37 PM||||that reminds me. I wouldn't mind getting an 8,000 RPM tach and a 240kph speedo. <P>a while ago someone posted a circuit on the forum that allowed a speedometer to be recalibrated to read up to any speed... if you could post this again, I'm sure a lot of people here would jump on it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Also, how would I recalibrate the tach to read higher?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||12-28-2000||11:03 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/8grand.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/8grand.jpg</A> <P><BR>8000 rpm tach. from what I have seen the Tach will go to what ever it is revved to. A friend of mine had a q4 conversion and it would go right off the tach. My gauges look perfect!!. My install required 2 sheets of plastic , a white background and the gauges themselves that are printed on clear plastic. The set I'm installing tomorrow on a friends GT are printed on a plastic type paper. IT's mositure resistant. an easier process and cheaper!. I can also do this in black like the original if you want to keep the factory look<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...||||reg||1
